    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 358\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7423, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the New York state urban development corporation\n      act, in relation to assistance for certain small businesses\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Empire State Development Corporation (ESD)\nto provide financial assistance to dry  cleaners  and  nail  salons  for\ncapital infrastructure projects.\n \n  I  vetoed  an  identical bill last year because New York State already\nprovides a variety of financial resources to assist all types  of  small\nbusinesses,  including dry cleaners and nail salons, in making necessary\ncapital upgrades to their facilities; (see Veto 212, Laws of 2017). As I\nnoted in my prior message, ESD's existing programs include (i) Community\nDevelopment  Financial  Institution  (CDFI)  Assistance  Program,  which\nprovides  microloans  to  small businesses that often do not qualify for\nbank loans, (ii) Small Business  Revolving  Loan  Fund,  which  provides\ngrants  for capital projects to small retail, service, and manufacturing\nbusinesses that have difficulty  accessing  credit  markets,  and  (iii)\nCapital  Access Program. All of these programs provide increased financ-\ning opportunities for small businesses, including dry cleaner  and  nail\nsalon  businesses,  throughout  the State. Moreover, because the bill is\nestablishing a new grant program with no funding  source,  it  would  be\nbetter addressed in the context of the annual State budget.\n \n  For  the  foregoing reasons, while I remain committed to ensuring that\nsmall businesses have access to capital funding, I must veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
